# Tracked data files must check out byte-identically on every platform.
#
# The SHA-256 digest of each declared data tree is recorded as run provenance in
# data/snapshots/SNAPSHOT_VERSIONS.json and re-verified on every load. Git's
# autocrlf translation would otherwise hand a Windows checkout CRLF bytes and a
# Linux checkout LF bytes for byte-for-byte identical content, so snapshot
# verification would fail on whichever platform did not record the digest.
#
# Scoped to data/ deliberately: these are the trees whose bytes are hashed.
# Source and documentation line endings are left to each contributor's setup.
data/** text eol=lf

# Binary payloads under data/: never translate.
data/**/*.png binary
data/**/*.gz binary
data/**/*.bz2 binary
data/**/*.zip binary
